% Architecture section 17: a predicate is (name, arity), so foo/1 and foo/2
% are unrelated and neither is an inconsistent use of the other.  A predicate
% may also have both facts and rules, which seed and extend one relation.
foo(a).
foo(X) :-
    bar(X).

foo(a, b).
foo(X, Y) :-
    bar(X),
    bar(Y).

bar(z).
